# Line endings, for the files where they are not cosmetic.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For source that is only ever read that
# is harmless. For a file something else has to *execute* it is not: a shell
# script with CRLF endings fails on Linux and macOS with the memorable and
# useless `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`, and the hook below is committed
# precisely so other clones can use it.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
